# The guardrail image is built from the repository root because it packages modules from
# several top-level directories. Send only its runtime files; Terraform provider caches
# alone are hundreds of MB and must never become Docker build context.
#
# THIS FILE HAS TO BE UPDATED WHENEVER A PACKAGED DIRECTORY IS RENAMED. It still said
# guardrail_service/ after that package became services/llm_pipeline/, so `services/`
# was excluded from the build context and `COPY services/ services/` failed with
# "/services": not found -- an error that points at the Dockerfile and is caused here.
**
!guardrails/
!guardrails/**
!prompt/
!prompt/**
!rag/
!rag/**
!services/
!services/**
!data/
!data/xanhsm_retrieval_mock/
!data/xanhsm_retrieval_mock/corpus/
!data/xanhsm_retrieval_mock/corpus/retrieval_corpus.jsonl
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
